---
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import '../global.css'; 
---

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <title>The Apocryphon of John: Decoding the Gnostic Cosmology | Sacred History</title>
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Cinzel:wght@400;600;700&family=Cormorant+Garamond:ital,wght@0,400;0,600;1,400&family=Montserrat:wght@400;500;600&family=Oswald:wght@500;700&family=Playfair+Display:ital,wght@0,400;0,600;1,400&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
  </head>
  <body>
    <Header />

    <main class="site-wrapper section theme-reconciling" style="background: rgba(5, 10, 18, 1); padding-bottom: 80px;">

      <!-- WAYFINDING CONDUIT -->
      <nav class="shsq-wayfinding-conduit reveal" aria-label="Article Navigation" style="margin-top: 40px; max-width: 900px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; padding: 0 20px;">
        <ul class="breadcrumb-trail" style="list-style: none; padding: 0; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 10px; color: var(--shsq-gold, #C6A664); font-family: 'Cinzel', serif; text-transform: uppercase; font-size: 0.85rem;">
          <li><a href="/the-escape-matrix/" style="color: inherit; text-decoration: none; transition: color 0.3s ease;">↵ Master Grid</a></li>
          <li class="separator" aria-hidden="true" style="color: var(--shsq-muted, #888888);">/</li>
          <li><a href="/sacred-history/" style="color: inherit; text-decoration: none; transition: color 0.3s ease;">Sacred History Archive</a></li>
          <li class="separator" aria-hidden="true" style="color: var(--shsq-muted, #888888);">/</li>
          <li class="current-node" aria-current="page" style="color: var(--shsq-parchment, #E6E6E6);">Apocryphon of John</li>
        </ul>
      </nav>

      <!-- HERO HEADER -->
      <header class="article-header reveal" style="margin-bottom: 40px; max-width: 900px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; padding: 0 20px;">
        <span class="section-eyebrow" style="color: var(--shsq-silver, #B0B8C0); font-size: 0.9rem; letter-spacing: 3px; text-transform: uppercase;">Hub I: Gnostic Gnosis</span>
        <h1 class="article-title" style="color: var(--shsq-gold, #C6A664); font-family: 'Cinzel', serif; font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3.5rem); margin-top: 15px; margin-bottom: 25px; line-height: 1.2;">The Apocryphon of John</h1>
        <p class="article-lead" style="color: var(--shsq-parchment, #E6E6E6); font-size: 1.2rem; line-height: 1.8; font-style: italic;">
          The foundational architecture of the Sethian cosmology and the mechanics of Archontic containment.
        </p>
      </header>

      <!-- ARTICLE BODY -->
      <article class="shsq-article-body reveal reveal-delay-1" style="max-width: 800px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 20px;">

        <!-- CALLOUT BOX -->
        <aside class="shsq-callout" style="border-left: 4px solid var(--shsq-gold, #C6A664); background: rgba(198, 166, 100, 0.05); padding: 30px; margin-bottom: 50px;" aria-label="Key Takeaways">
          <h3 style="color: var(--shsq-gold, #C6A664); font-family: 'Cinzel', serif; letter-spacing: 2px; text-transform: uppercase; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 20px; font-size: 1.4rem;">Key Takeaways</h3>
          <ul style="color: var(--shsq-parchment, #E6E6E6); font-family: 'Montserrat', sans-serif; font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.8; margin-bottom: 0; padding-left: 20px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 15px;">
            <li>The <em>Apocryphon of John</em> survives in four independent Coptic manuscripts, including both "long" and "short" recensions found in the Nag Hammadi Library and the Berlin Gnostic Codex.</li>
            <li>Textual evidence suggests the original Greek composition dates to the mid-second century, as Bishop Irenaeus of Lyon explicitly polemicized against its doctrines in his treatise <em>Adversus Haereses</em> around 180 CE.</li>
            <li>The cosmological framework operates on a strict structural dualism, contrasting the transcendent Pleroma, ruled by the Invisible Virgin Spirit, with the deficient material Kenoma, governed by the ignorant Demiurge, Yaldabaoth.</li>
            <li>The text posits that humanity is subjugated by universal fate (<em>Heimarmene</em>) and a synthetic psychological overlay known as the <em>Antimimon Pneuma</em> (Counterfeit Spirit), designed by the Archons to induce spiritual amnesia.</li>
            <li>Salvation within this system is not achieved through orthodox obedience or vicarious atonement, but through gnosis—an anamnetic awakening triggered by the descent of a heavenly Illuminator who restores the divine spark.</li>
          </ul>
        </aside>

        <!-- MAIN PROSE -->
        <div class="entry-content" style="color: var(--shsq-parchment, #E6E6E6); font-family: 'Montserrat', sans-serif; font-size: 1.1rem; line-height: 1.8;">

          <h2 style="color: var(--shsq-gold, #C6A664); font-family: 'Cinzel', serif; font-size: 2rem; margin-top: 50px; margin-bottom: 20px; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(198, 166, 100, 0.2); padding-bottom: 10px;">Historical Context and Provenance</h2>
          <p style="margin-bottom: 20px;">
            For nearly two millennia, the historical understanding of the religious movements collectively termed "Gnosticism" relied almost exclusively upon the polemical writings of their orthodox opponents. Church authorities such as Irenaeus of Lyon, Hippolytus of Rome, and Epiphanius of Salamis documented the beliefs of these marginalized sects primarily to refute them, categorizing their cosmologies as dangerous deviations from the emerging apostolic tradition. The <em>Apocryphon of John</em> (frequently referred to as the <em>Secret Book of John</em>) stands as the primary foundational document of the Sethian Gnostic tradition—a sect that identified itself as the "unshakable race" or the "seed of Seth."
          </p>
          <p style="margin-bottom: 20px;">
            The text emerged during a period of intense religious ferment in the Mediterranean and Near East during the second century CE. This era was characterized by the syncretic blending of Hellenistic philosophy (particularly Middle Platonism), Jewish apocalyptic literature, and early Christian theology. Scholars generally recognize the <em>Apocryphon of John</em> as a critical transitional document that utilizes "inverted exegesis" of the Hebrew Bible—specifically the opening chapters of Genesis—to address theodicy and the problem of evil.
          </p>

          <h2 style="color: var(--shsq-gold, #C6A664); font-family: 'Cinzel', serif; font-size: 2rem; margin-top: 50px; margin-bottom: 20px; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(198, 166, 100, 0.2); padding-bottom: 10px;">Manuscript Tradition and Translation History</h2>
          <p style="margin-bottom: 20px;">
            The modern recovery of the <em>Apocryphon of John</em> is a testament to the complex transmission history of ancient esoteric documents. The first major breakthrough occurred in 1896 when the German Egyptologist Carl Schmidt acquired the Berlin Gnostic Codex, containing an independent Coptic translation. However, it was the monumental discovery of the Nag Hammadi Library in December 1945 that revolutionized the study of the text, unearthing three additional Coptic translations preserved in Codices II, III, and IV.
          </p>
          <p style="margin-bottom: 20px;">
            The variations between these recensions provide invaluable data regarding the redaction history of the text. The manuscript evidence suggests that the <em>Apocryphon</em> was not a static document but a fluid, living mythology that was continually edited, expanded, and Christianized by successive generations of scribes.
          </p>

          <h2 style="color: var(--shsq-gold, #C6A664); font-family: 'Cinzel', serif; font-size: 2rem; margin-top: 50px; margin-bottom: 20px; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(198, 166, 100, 0.2); padding-bottom: 10px;">Structural Mechanics of the Cosmology</h2>
          
          <h3 style="color: var(--shsq-silver, #B0B8C0); font-family: 'Cinzel', serif; font-size: 1.5rem; margin-top: 40px; margin-bottom: 15px;">Apophatic Theology and the Monad</h3>
          <p style="margin-bottom: 20px;">
            The cosmological architecture begins in the Pleroma, the absolute fullness of the transcendent spiritual realm. At the apex exists the ultimate deity, the Invisible Virgin Spirit, the Monad, or the One. The text employs a rigorous apophatic theology, defining the supreme God strictly by what it is not. From the self-reflection of this invisible spirit emanates the first power: Barbelo, the perfect divine forethought (<em>Pronoia</em>).
          </p>

          <h3 style="color: var(--shsq-silver, #B0B8C0); font-family: 'Cinzel', serif; font-size: 1.5rem; margin-top: 40px; margin-bottom: 15px;">The Demiurgic Fault of Sophia</h3>
          <p style="margin-bottom: 20px;">
            The harmony of the Pleroma is shattered by a cosmological crisis initiated by the lowest of the divine Aeons, Sophia (Wisdom). Because her creative act is driven by unilateral presumption rather than divine equilibrium, her offspring is deformed. This entity is the Demiurge, Yaldabaoth. Isolated in the abyss, he arrogates absolute power to himself, using a portion of stolen light-power from his mother to organize the material cosmos.
          </p>
          <blockquote style="border-left: 4px solid var(--shsq-gold, #C6A664); margin: 30px 0; padding: 20px 30px; background: rgba(198, 166, 100, 0.05); font-family: 'Cinzel', serif; font-size: 1.15rem; font-style: italic; color: var(--shsq-gold, #C6A664); line-height: 1.8;">
            <p style="margin-bottom: 0;">"I am a jealous God, and there is no other God beside me."</p>
          </blockquote>

          <h3 style="color: var(--shsq-silver, #B0B8C0); font-family: 'Cinzel', serif; font-size: 1.5rem; margin-top: 40px; margin-bottom: 15px;">Anthropogony and Archontic Containment</h3>
          <p style="margin-bottom: 20px;">
            Hearing Yaldabaoth's blasphemy, the divine forces intervene. Emissaries from the Pleroma advise Yaldabaoth to breathe his spirit into the inert, newly formed Adam. When the Demiurge complies, he unwittingly transfers the divine light-power he had taken from Sophia into the human body. Recognizing their error, the Archons cast Adam into the lowest regions and reconstruct his physical flesh into a dense biological prison.
          </p>

          <h3 style="color: var(--shsq-silver, #B0B8C0); font-family: 'Cinzel', serif; font-size: 1.5rem; margin-top: 40px; margin-bottom: 15px;">Heimarmene and the Antimimon Pneuma</h3>
          <p style="margin-bottom: 20px;">
            To maintain control, Yaldabaoth and his Archons institute a system of cosmic administration: <em>Heimarmene</em> (Universal Fate). Furthermore, to suppress the awakening of the divine Spirit, they engineer an artificial psychological overlay known as the <em>Antimimon Pneuma</em> (the Counterfeit Spirit), plunging the soul into the waters of forgetfulness and ensuring the cycle of reincarnation.
          </p>

          <h3 style="color: var(--shsq-silver, #B0B8C0); font-family: 'Cinzel', serif; font-size: 1.5rem; margin-top: 40px; margin-bottom: 15px;">Soteriology and the Luminous Epinoia</h3>
          <p style="margin-bottom: 20px;">
            Liberation is attained strictly through gnosis. The perfect Forethought of the All descends into the realm of darkness, awakening the dormant Spirit, shattering the programming of the Counterfeit Spirit, and sealing the enlightened souls with the waters of life, securing their safe passage back to the Pleroma.
          </p>

        </div>

        <hr class="shsq-divider reveal" aria-hidden="true" style="border: 0; border-top: 1px solid rgba(198, 166, 100, 0.3); margin: 60px 0;">

        <nav class="article-pagination reveal reveal-delay-2" style="text-align: center; margin-top: 40px; margin-bottom: 40px;">
          <div class="pagination-link next-pillar">
            <span class="pagination-label" style="display: block; color: var(--shsq-silver, #B0B8C0); font-size: 0.85rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 2px; margin-bottom: 15px;">Advance to Archive Entry</span>
            <a href="/sacred-history/reality-of-the-rulers/" class="brutalist-btn" style="display: inline-block; background: transparent; border: 1px solid var(--shsq-gold, #C6A664); padding: 15px 30px; color: var(--shsq-gold, #C6A664); font-weight: bold; text-decoration: none; font-family: 'Cinzel', serif; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 2px; transition: all 0.3s ease;" onmouseover="this.style.background='var(--shsq-gold)'; this.style.color='#050A12';" onmouseout="this.style.background='transparent'; this.style.color='var(--shsq-gold)';">
              The Reality of the Rulers →
            </a>
          </div>
        </nav>

        <div class="shsq-footer-note" style="border-top: 1px solid rgba(198, 166, 100, 0.1); padding-top: 30px; text-align: center; color: rgba(176, 184, 192, 0.6); font-size: 0.85rem; font-style: italic;">
          <p style="margin: 0;">An Exoteric Archive: Methodology &amp; Provenance · Guided by Sophia Mysterion.</p>
        </div>

      </article>

    </main>

    <Footer />

    <!-- GLOBAL CSS INJECTION TO GUARANTEE REVEAL WORKS -->
    <style is:global>
      .reveal {
        opacity: 0;
        transform: translateY(30px);
        transition: opacity 0.8s cubic-bezier(0.5, 0, 0, 1), transform 0.8s cubic-bezier(0.5, 0, 0, 1);
      }
      .reveal.visible {
        opacity: 1;
        transform: translateY(0);
      }
      .reveal-delay-1 { transition-delay: 0.15s; }
      .reveal-delay-2 { transition-delay: 0.3s; }
    </style>

    <!-- BULLETPROOF CLIENT-SIDE SCROLL REVEAL SCRIPT -->
    <script>
      function initReveal() {
        const observerOptions = {
          root: null,
          rootMargin: '0px',
          threshold: 0.1
        };

        const observer = new IntersectionObserver((entries) => {
          entries.forEach(entry => {
            if (entry.isIntersecting) {
              entry.target.classList.add('visible');
              observer.unobserve(entry.target); // Stops observing once revealed
            }
          });
        }, observerOptions);

        const revealElements = document.querySelectorAll('.reveal');
        revealElements.forEach(el => observer.observe(el));
      }

      // Fires on initial hard load
      document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', initReveal);
      
      // Fires on Astro View Transition navigation
      document.addEventListener('astro:page-load', initReveal);
    </script>
  </body>
</html>